{"id": 36, "ts": 1780129123.507585, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019d like to explain why I\u2019m still leaning toward Candidate\u202fB.\u202fFrom my notes, B is very conscientious and handles stress exceptionally well \u2013 both core to operational reliability and stress resilience for long\u2011distance flights. He also assesses weather conditions accurately and has excellent computer skills, which speak to his technical and cognitive competence.\nMy main reservation is his professional communication: he makes nasty remarks about colleagues and has a relatively weak memory for numbers.\u202fThese are legitimate concerns for crew cooperation and information accuracy, but they are more specific and potentially remediable than the broader issues I see with Candidate\u202fC.\u202fC keeps calm in a crisis and makes quick, correct decisions, yet he is regarded as egocentric, struggles to communicate ideas, and is not very willing to pursue further education \u2013 all of which raise serious doubts about his long\u2011term adaptability and teamwork in a cockpit environment.\nThus, while both B and C have notable strengths, B\u2019s reliability and stress handling give him a stronger overall fit, and his communication shortfall, though important, appears less likely to jeopardize safety than C\u2019s pervasive cooperation and development concerns.\u202fWe still need to bring Candidate\u202fA and D into the discussion to ensure full coverage, but at this stage B remains my preferred choice."}
